## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop**: `Game` holds resources/state/colonists/map; `endTurn()` calls fireEvent→produceResources→consumeResources→updateMorale→ashstorm in fixed order. `mulberry32()`→`this.rng()` used in createColonist/fireEvent/ashstorm, but `generateMap()` uses raw `(seed+i*73)%1000` instead of `rng()` — not all randomness goes through the PRNG. Score: 1

**F2 – Map**: 8x8 (`map.length===64`); `buildBuilding()` checks `b.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `getAdjacencyBonus()` multiplies output via `(1+adjBonus)` in `produceResources()`. Score: 2

**F3 – Economy**: ore→metal (mine/forge) and ash→soil→food (soilMaker/greenhouse) chains; `Math.min(state.caps.x, ...)` caps everywhere. Score: 2

**F4 – Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job/assignedBuilding; `avgSkill`/`fatigueModifier` read in `produceResources()`. Score: 2

**F5 – Needs**: `consumeResources()` computes shortfall, lowers `c.morale`; but `produceResources()` never reads `c.morale` in the output formula — required link missing. Score: 1

**F6 – Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH`; `research()` enforces prereq/availability, deducts cost; construction/shielding read in `ashstorm()`, medicine in `updateMorale()`; `efficiency`'s claimed effect is never read anywhere. Score: 2

**F7 – Events**: 10 entries in `EVENTS`; `fireEvent()` does weighted selection; 4 events (morale_crisis, merchant, sickness, pests) have distinct choice effects; `state.firedEvents` gives 10-turn cooldown. Score: 2

**F8 – Trade**: `caravanPrices` set once in `initPrices()`, never mutated by turns/stock; `trade()` supports buy/sell; no caravan inventory cap; `globalDemand` declared but unused. Score: 1

**F9 – Hazard**: `ashstorm()` fires every 12 turns, severity grows with turn, damages `b.health`; construction/shielding reduce damage; but `produceResources()` never reads building `health`, and no repair function exists anywhere. Score: 1

**F10 – Save/load**: `serialize()` JSON-dumps full state to textarea; `deserialize()` try/catch parses pasted JSON, returns `'Invalid JSON'` shown by `doLoad()`. Score: 2

**F11 – End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water>=100`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`) both reachable; `renderMap()` shows WIN/LOSE text, but no numeric score computed from multiple state values. Score: 1

**F12 – UI**: `switchTab()` toggles panels; log lines show `T${e.turn}`; `.tooltip` shows building/terrain info; keydown handles Space/1-6; `@media(max-width:600px)` adapts layout. Score: 2

**F13 – Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts 15 real invariants (caps, ranges, prereqs, hash round-trip); `runBench()` runs 200 `g.endTurn()` calls headlessly and prints start/end hash. Score: 2

**G1**: `research()` sets `BUILDINGS.forge.unlocked=true`, gated in `buildBuilding()`, enabling new production; no research effect is read inside `produceResources()` as a yield multiplier. Score: 2

**G2**: shortfall→morale drop implemented in `consumeResources()`, but `produceResources()` never reads `c.morale` — final link absent. Score: 1

**G3**: `ashstorm()` damages `b.health`, but `produceResources()` never reads it and no repair function exists anywhere. Score: 1

**G4**: `caravanPrices` fixed at init, never updated by turn count or `resources`; `globalDemand` unused. Score: 0

**G5**: morale_crisis/merchant/sickness/pests choices each mutate `g.resources`/colonist fields distinctly, not just log text. Score: 4

